---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const repo = 'https://github.com/pjdoland/coachbook/blob/main';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About this archive"
  description="Editorial standards, scope, sourcing, and how to flag a correction."
>
  <p class="standfirst">Colophon</p>
  <h1>About this archive</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    coachbook is an independent reference archive of vintage Coach
    Leatherware, 1941–2002. Built from free public sources with
    citation discipline. Not affiliated with Coach, Inc.
  </p>

  <h2>Scope</h2>
  <p>
    Vintage Coach starts in 1941, when Gail Leather Products opens in a
    Manhattan loft. It runs through the Bonnie Cashin years
    (1962–1974), the Cahn-family ownership (1961–1985), the Sara Lee
    era (1985–2001), and the Reed Krakoff transition (1996 onward). It
    ends, for our purposes, around 2002 — the season the original
    heritage silhouettes (Willis, Court, Companion Flap, Daypack) drop
    out of the catalog and Legacy West replaces them.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Krakoff transition is treated as <em>contrast only</em>: in
    scope where it bounds the NYC era, not as the archive's main
    subject. See <a href={`${repo}/PLAN.md`}>PLAN.md</a> for the
    full scope rules.
  </p>

  <h2>Editorial standards</h2>
  <p>Every claim in this archive carries two things:</p>
  <dl>
    <dt>A confidence tag</dt>
    <dd>
      <span class="chip" data-confidence="confirmed">confirmed</span> ·
      <span class="chip" data-confidence="likely">likely</span> ·
      <span class="chip" data-confidence="tentative">tentative</span> ·
      <span class="chip" data-confidence="disputed">disputed</span>
    </dd>
    <dt>A source citation</dt>
    <dd>
      A short, stable source ID (e.g. <code>coach-catalogs-1960-1989</code>)
      that resolves in the registry to a tiered, dated, archive-snapshotted
      reference.
    </dd>
  </dl>
  <p>
    Tier 1 is primary documents — Coach catalogs, SEC filings, USPTO
    records. Tier 2 is reputable secondary sources — encyclopedia
    entries, trade press, museum archives. Tier 3 is community
    references — collector blogs, PurseForum threads. Tier 4 is
    listing evidence — eBay, Etsy, individual auction lots. Tier 1
    overrides Tier 2; Tier 2 overrides Tier 3 unless triangulated.
    Full rules: <a href={`${repo}/STYLE.md`}>STYLE.md</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Why 2002?</h2>
  <p>
    The 2002 Autumn catalog is the last in-scope catalog. By that
    point Willis 9927, Court 9870, Companion Flap 9076, and the
    original Daypack 9791 have all been retired and the Krakoff-era
    Legacy West sub-collection has replaced them with re-numbered,
    re-named silhouettes. After 2002 the archive's subject — vintage
    NYC-era Coach — no longer exists as a current-season concept.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Trust comes from documenting being wrong. Every correction is
    dated and logged in <a href={`${base}errata/`}>errata</a>, with a
    before/after and the source that surfaced the error. Nothing is
    silently overwritten.
  </p>
  <p>
    To flag a correction:
    <a href="https://github.com/pjdoland/coachbook/issues/new?title=Correction%3A%20"
       rel="noopener">open a GitHub issue</a>
    with the page, the claim, and the source you'd cite against it.
  </p>

  <h2>Method</h2>
  <p>
    The catalog corpus (107 Coach catalogs, 1960–2020) was deep-read
    season-by-season across research streams M, N, O, P, Q (one stream
    per period). Each stream produced a primary-source-cited research
    file in <code>research/</code>; corrections to model and
    authentication entries flow from there.
  </p>
  <p>
    Code, data, and the full editorial method are public at
    <a href="https://github.com/pjdoland/coachbook">github.com/pjdoland/coachbook</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The work</h2>
  <p>
    Built and edited by PJ Doland. Not a commercial project; not for
    sale. If the archive helps you authenticate, date, or research a
    specific bag, that's the entire point.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .standfirst {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--ink-quiet);
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 56ch;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
</style>
